-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
Optimize VGA progress bar to avoid redundant memory writes

[Feature Description]
The UpdateProgressBar function in BaseIGpuInfoLib was rewriting the
entire progress bar from 0% to the current percentage on every update,
causing redundant VGA memory writes. For example, updating from 10% to
50% would redraw columns 0-50 instead of only drawing the new 10-50%
portion.

This optimization introduces incremental progress bar updates by storing
the previous progress percentage in IGpuDataHob->PreviousProgressBar and
only filling the delta between the previous and current positions. This
significantly reduces VGA memory writes and improves performance during
memory initialization progress display.

The optimization applies to both VGA Text Mode 3 (80x25) and Graphics
Mode 12 (640x480) with special handling for clearing (percentage = 0)
which always fills the entire bar.

Changes include:
- Added PreviousProgressBar field to IGPU_DATA_HOB structure
- Modified UpdateProgressBar to track and use previous progress position
- Implemented incremental fill logic for both Mode 3 and Mode 12

