-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
Fix FSPAPI UART Pin Mux cause boot assert

[Issue Description]
FSPAPI BIOS encounters an assertion failure when using Debug ROM.
The debug output shows:
ASSERT NvlPcdGpioNativeLib.c(200): PinMux == 0

[Resolution]
Investigation revealed that SerialIoUartTxPinMuxPolicy[0] was being
overwritten in the UpdateLpssPchIoeConfig function with IOE GPIO
configuration.

To resolve this issue, IoeSerialIoUartTxPinMuxPolicy[] has been
added to the FSPS UPD structure.

IoeSerialIoUartTxPinMuxPolicy is now used exclusively for configuring
IOE GPIO, preventing the overwrite condition that caused the assertion.

